      "title": "Health officials in turmoil over 11th-hour backflip on aged care algorithm override powers, emails reveal",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/17/australian-home-support-assessment-algorithm-aged-care",
      "description": "<p>Ministers given emergency briefing about changes to algorithm decisions just three days before tool rollout</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Senior department of health officials were in turmoil before the rollout of an algorithm to determine funding packages for older Australians, after discovering legislation had been drafted so rigidly that the tool could not legally be overridden by aged care assessors.</p><p>Emails published under freedom of information (FoI) by the department of health, disability and ageing show that, despite assessors long receiving reassurance from the department that they would have powers to change incorrect algorithm decisions, officials realised at the 11th hour this would violate proposed regulations.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/17/australian-home-support-assessment-algorithm-aged-care\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-16T15:00:24"
    },
    {
      "title": "Bondi attacks prompt creation of new institute for emergency care of children in NSW",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/17/bondi-attacks-prompt-creation-of-new-institute-for-emergency-care-of-children-in-nsw",
      "description": "<p>NSW Institute for Paediatric Trauma will help doctors, researchers and specialists prepare for trauma cases</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">new political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>A new institute dedicated to improving emergency medical care for severely injured children will be established in New South Wales following recent high-profile trauma events in the state.</p><p>Based at the Sydney Children’s hospital in Randwick, the NSW Institute for Paediatric Trauma will bring together clinicians, researchers and specialists to deliver advanced training and simulations across the health system.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/17/bondi-attacks-prompt-creation-of-new-institute-for-emergency-care-of-children-in-nsw\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-16T14:01:21"
    },
    {
      "title": "‘It’s how Jean does business’: fugitive developer left Jeremy Greenwood ‘high and dry’, Icac hears",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/16/jeremy-greenwood-icac-evidence-perrottet-payments-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Greenwood denies that invoices for almost $1m sent in a single day in September 2021 were ‘bogus accounts’ to cover up political donations</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/16/pauline-hanson-one-nation-labor-anthony-albanese-artificial-intelligence-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>A Liberal factional figure has been left “high and dry” by fugitive property developer Jean Nassif, but did not chase him for payments because “it’s how Jean does business”, New South Wales’ anti-corruption watchdog has heard.</p><p>Jeremy Greenwood returned to the Independent Commission Against Corruption (Icac) on Wednesday after Nassif made an explosive video appearance from his Beirut bedroom on Monday and Tuesday. Nassif declared he was <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/15/jean-nassif-icac-evidence-fugitive-developer-ntwnfb\">“not corrupt”</a>.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/sep/16/jeremy-greenwood-icac-evidence-perrottet-payments-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-16T08:41:09"
    },
    {
      "title": "Minns says Molly Ticehurst’s murderer deserved longer sentence for ‘vicious’ crime’ – as it happened",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/16/pauline-hanson-one-nation-labor-anthony-albanese-artificial-intelligence-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>This blog is now closed</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">new political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p><strong>Sports precinct funding report reveals a ‘pattern of behaviour’, Wilson says</strong></p><p><strong>Tim Wilson</strong> says there are questions for Labor to answer over an ABC report which says health minister <strong>Mark Butler’s</strong> office asked an Adelaide council to put forward a $6m sports precinct upgrade for federal funding before any detailed costings or formal planning had been done.</p><p>I think what we’re now seeing is a pattern of behaviour. The prime minister gave a grant to a golf course in his electorate just around the corner from his home, of which he was a member, which he failed to declare. Now we have the health minister, the next wannabe prime minister, doing exactly the same thing.</p><p>That’s a difficult thing to do. However, I think one way to do it is to ensure that Muslim leaders are at the centre of any such discussion and guide that discussion in a way that Australian Muslims as a whole do not feel targeted.</p><p>Because there is a real risk when you have a discussion about extremist Islam, you have a real risk that Muslims as a whole feel under pressure. Equally, if you don’t have that discussion, you play into the hands of extremists at the other end of the spectrum.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/sep/16/pauline-hanson-one-nation-labor-anthony-albanese-artificial-intelligence-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-09-16T08:11:31"
    },
    {
